  {
    "id": "question 4949",
    "verdict": "ambiguous",
    "correct_option": null,
    "evidence": "Per IEEE 802.11, the PS-Poll's purpose itself is to retrieve buffered frames; the NAV is updated as a side effect ('stations receiving a PS-Poll frame update the NAV by the short interframe space plus the time required to transmit an ACK'). The marked option 'synchronize ACK frame transmission' doesn't directly map to either the PS-Poll purpose or the NAV update purpose — defensible answers could be options 2 or 5.",
    "source": "IEEE 802.11"
  },
  {
